I sold batteries at a locally owned small business and half the business we sold were car batteries. Ill tell you something about car batteries and its that they bring out the worst in people for whatever reason. I have countless stories of seemingly rational smart people being complete irrational assholes over absolutely nothing. For context i was knowledgeable and super courteous and would do whatever i could to help someone if it was in my power. We sold arguably the best batteries you can buy and had long free replacement warranties for $100-$120. We had an economy version which was also a good battery but with a 3-6 month warranty for 75-90 bucks. We were cheaper than literally anywhere aside from walmart at times or tractor supply but people expected us to be even cheaper. The amount of people that would scoff at our prices and instantly become a complete dickhead was higher than sounds believable.  People would somehow logic that  they were doing me a favor by shopping with us because we were a small business and they were entitled compensation in the form of cheaper prices. I found alot of People regularly would tell me they were going to get it cheaper somewhere else or trying to haggle because we were supposedly friends from the one other time they were in the store. Then when i courteously explain i cant budge on the price and why they would usually double down and keep trying to haggle but it rarely ended with them just saying " ok that sound reasonable". Alot of the time it did end with them having to come back in and buy from us when they realized i was right but they would never acknowledge it. If someone just came in and was a genuinely reasonable person that didnt give us unwarranted shit it was seen as a nice surprise.  .

Haggle if you must and i didnt mind the first ask but you are an asshole if you keep making me tell you no again to lowering the price. This happened daily and was a constant cause of bullshit. It definitly had to do with the fact we were a locally owned small business but alot of people loved telling us they "supported small business" while leaving to go to walmart to get a battery that is the same price as the one i have on the counter.

